Setup the complete MCP platform including:
- Kubernetes cluster initialization
- Internal container registry deployment (Docker Registry)
- Operator deployment
- Ingress controller configuration

The platform deploys an internal Docker registry by default, which teams
will use to push and pull container images.

Usage:
  mcp-runtime setup [flags]

Flags:
      --acme-email string                    Contact email for Let's Encrypt (HTTP-01 via cert-manager). Mutually exclusive with --tls-cluster-issuer. Overrides env MCP_ACME_EMAIL
      --acme-staging                         Use Let's Encrypt staging CA (also set MCP_ACME_STAGING=1)
      --context string                       Kubernetes context to use
      --docs-path string                     Public path that redirects to the configured documentation URL (default "/docs")
      --docs-url string                      HTTPS documentation destination used by the docs route and dashboard links (default "https://mcpruntime.org/docs/")
      --env-file string                      Path to an env file to source before setup (e.g. config/deployments/mcpruntime-org.env); variables already in the environment are not overridden
      --external-registry-password string    External/provisioned registry password for --registry-mode external (prefer PROVISIONED_REGISTRY_PASSWORD for shells)
      --external-registry-url string         External/provisioned registry URL for --registry-mode external (overrides PROVISIONED_REGISTRY_URL and registry provision config)
      --external-registry-username string    External/provisioned registry username for --registry-mode external
      --force-ingress-install                Force repo-managed ingress install when only an IngressClass exists; refuses active external Traefik
      --grafana-path-prefix string           Public admin-only Grafana path prefix (default "/grafana")
  -h, --help                                 help for setup
      --ingress string                       Ingress controller to install automatically during setup (traefik|none) (default "traefik")
      --ingress-manifest string              Manifest to apply when installing the ingress controller (default "config/ingress/overlays/http")
      --kubeconfig string                    Path to kubeconfig file (default: ~/.kube/config; auto-detects /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml on k3s hosts)
      --mcp-auth-connector string            Provider connector name to activate (requires --mcp-auth-connectors-file)
      --mcp-auth-connectors-file string      Provider connector JSON file for the bundled mcp-auth authorization server
      --mcp-auth-issuer-url string           Public HTTPS issuer URL for the bundled mcp-auth authorization server (defaults to https://auth.<MCP_PLATFORM_DOMAIN>/mcp-auth)
      --mcp-auth-resource-url strings        Optional initial resource URI for the bundled mcp-auth server; the operator reconciles this list from OAuth MCPServer audiences
      --mcp-auth-server-image string         Container image for the optional bundled mcp-auth authorization server (default "docker.io/princekrroshan01/mcp-auth-server:0.4.4")
      --mcp-auth-signing-key-secret string   Secret holding the mcp-auth RSA signing key as private-key.pem (required outside --test-mode)
      --mcp-auth-tls-secret string           Override the managed TLS Secret for the bundled mcp-auth ingress (default: mcp-auth-server-tls)
      --mtls-cluster-issuer string           Enable adapter client-certificate authentication on gateway server routes using this workload ClusterIssuer (requires --with-tls). Name an enterprise issuer, or the bundled mcp-runtime-ca to have setup provision it. Test mode defaults to mcp-runtime-ca. Production must also set MCP_TRUST_DOMAIN. Overrides env MCP_SETUP_MTLS_CLUSTER_ISSUER
      --operator-leader-elect                Override operator leader election when set
      --operator-metrics-addr string         Operator metrics bind address (default: :8080 from manager.yaml)
      --operator-probe-addr string           Operator health probe bind address (default: :8081 from manager.yaml)
      --parallel-builds                      Build and publish setup images in parallel; keeps cluster, registry, TLS, and rollout sequencing unchanged
      --platform-mode string                 Platform access model (tenant|org|public). public exposes the catalog without login and lets signed-in users publish to the public preview namespace. (default "tenant")
      --platform-path-prefix string          Public dashboard path prefix (e.g. /platform); session and asset routes use this prefix (default "/")
      --pod-egress-cidrs string              Comma-separated destination CIDRs that team MCP servers may reach on TCP 443. Empty installs nothing. 0.0.0.0/0 is rejected. Private ranges also require --pod-egress-except-cidrs. Overrides env MCP_POD_EGRESS_CIDRS
      --pod-egress-except-cidrs string       Cluster pod and service CIDRs to keep out of --pod-egress-cidrs. Required when a destination is private. Overrides env MCP_POD_EGRESS_EXCEPT_CIDRS
      --provided-tls-secrets                 Use operator-created Kubernetes TLS Secrets instead of issuing certificates. Requires --with-tls; do not combine with --acme-email or --tls-cluster-issuer
      --registry-mode string                 Registry setup mode (auto|bundled-http|bundled-https|external). auto uses a provisioned registry config when present, otherwise the bundled registry (default "auto")
      --registry-path string                 Public registry browser entry path; Docker and Kubernetes clients still use /v2/ (default "/registry")
      --registry-storage string              Registry storage size (default: 20Gi) (default "20Gi")
      --registry-type string                 Registry type (docker; harbor coming soon) (default "docker")
      --skip-cert-manager-install            Do not install cert-manager; require CRDs to already exist
      --storage-mode string                  Storage mode for local/dev clusters (dynamic|hostpath). Use hostpath for single-node k3s/minikube/kind without a provisioner. (default "dynamic")
      --strict-prod                          Require production-style registry and TLS validation for non-test setup
      --test-mode                            Test mode for local Kind/dev installs; builds and pushes latest-tag runtime images, provisions a local workload mTLS issuer, and relaxes production guardrails
      --tls-cluster-issuer string            Use an existing cert-manager ClusterIssuer (e.g. internal CA; setup does not create it). Mutually exclusive with --acme-email. Overrides env MCP_SETUP_TLS_CLUSTER_ISSUER
      --with-mcp-auth-server                 Deploy the optional bundled mcp-auth authorization server; production requires a platform domain, connector, and TLS-enabled ingress
      --with-tls                             Enable TLS overlays (ingress/registry). Use --acme-email for public Let's Encrypt, --tls-cluster-issuer for an org ClusterIssuer, or the bundled mcp-runtime-ca private CA (no ACME) when neither is set
      --without-platform-stack               Skip deploying the bundled platform stack

Global Flags:
      --debug   Enable debug mode with structured error logging
